{# concept_diagram — a token-only, brand-agnostic conceptual diagram.

   Richard's reference decks lean on CONCEPTUAL DIAGRAMS (Venn / overlap /
   convergence figures) to make an argument visual instead of textual. This
   macro draws one from DATA only — no client literals, no hex, no font family;
   colours arrive via the `c-` token classes (styles/components.css), so it is
   brand-agnostic by construction and re-themes with the brand.

   kind == "convergence" (a 3-lobe Venn, mirroring the apex reference deck's
   myths-page figure): three soft overlapping discs, each labelled INSIDE its
   outer lobe, share ONE centre — the synthesis/root truth printed in the triple
   overlap. Used on the false-beliefs page (three Irrglauben → one Antwort).

   DATA CONTRACT (diagram dict):
     kind        : "convergence" (unknown kinds render nothing)
     nodes       : list of EXACTLY 3 short lobe labels (one per disc)
     center_lead : the centre's emphasised (bold) word — the payoff
     center      : optional rest of the centre phrase (after the bold lead)
     caption     : optional one-line caption under the figure

   No fabrication: every label is supplied by the preprocessor/data. With fewer
   than 3 nodes or no centre the macro renders nothing (graceful omit). #}
{% macro concept_diagram(diagram) %}
{%- if diagram and diagram.kind == 'convergence' and (diagram.nodes | length) >= 3 and (diagram.center_lead or diagram.center) -%}
<figure class="c-venn" role="img"
        aria-label="Konvergenz-Diagramm: {{ diagram.nodes[:3] | join(', ') }} → {{ diagram.center_lead }} {{ diagram.center }}">
  <div class="c-venn__stage">
    <span class="c-venn__lobe c-venn__lobe--a"><span class="c-venn__fill"></span></span>
    <span class="c-venn__lobe c-venn__lobe--b"><span class="c-venn__fill"></span></span>
    <span class="c-venn__lobe c-venn__lobe--c"><span class="c-venn__fill"></span></span>
    <span class="c-venn__label c-venn__label--a">{{ diagram.nodes[0] }}</span>
    <span class="c-venn__label c-venn__label--b">{{ diagram.nodes[1] }}</span>
    <span class="c-venn__label c-venn__label--c">{{ diagram.nodes[2] }}</span>
    <span class="c-venn__core">
      {%- if diagram.center_lead %}<strong>{{ diagram.center_lead }}</strong>{% endif -%}
      {%- if diagram.center %} {{ diagram.center }}{% endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
  {%- if diagram.caption %}
  <figcaption class="c-venn__caption">{{ diagram.caption }}</figcaption>
  {%- endif %}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
